---
title: Common raven
---
# Common raven

The common raven is the largest passerine, a heavy black crow with a shaggy
throat and a wedge-shaped tail. It is omnivorous and highly opportunistic, eating
carrion, eggs, grain and refuse, and it will follow a wolf pack or a hunter for
scraps. Pairs hold a territory year-round and perform rolling, tumbling display
flights over it. Ravens cache surplus food and take deliberate care to do so
unobserved, moving a cache if another raven was watching. See [[corvidae]].
